$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Labeling of 5-Cl-MNPP with Na125I in presence of phase transfer catalyst
(P.T.C.). In this round bottom flask, 10 μl Na125I (3.7 MBq) was taken to
dryness by a vacuum line. Then, the residue was dissolved by adding I ml
of DMF containing 5 mg of 5-Cl-MNPP followed by a known amount of
tetrabutyl ammonium bromide as phase transfer catalyst. The effect of the
quantity of tetrabutyl ammonium bromide (1-3 mg) in DMF on the labeling
yield of 125I-MNPP was studied at reflux. In each experiment the reaction
was allowed to proceed for a chosen time interval before the vessel
contents were removed for analysis. 5-125I-MNPP, yield: 95%. t½: 1.43
min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on catalyst,temp.,time, alternative
reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of 1-phenyl-3-methyl-4-nitro-5-125I- pyrazole (5-125I-MNPP)
as a possible cannabinoid receptor imaging agent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM El-Wetery, S.; El-Azoney, Kh. M.; El-Ghany, E. A.; El-Mohty, A. A.; Deeb,
A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Radioanalytical and Nuclear Chemistry (2001), 250(2), 335-345

