$DATUM Labeling of 5-Cl-MNPP with Na125I in dry state The reaction was carried
out in a v shaped reaction-vial that could be tightly closed by a screw
cap. Ten μl of 0.01M NaOH solution with about 3.7 MBq 125I-iodide was
introduced and evaporated to dryness on a vacuum line. Thereafter 5 mg of
5-Cl-MNPP were added. The reaction-vial was closed and heated at specific
temperature in an oil bath. The reaction was stopped by cooling vial in
an ice bath. The residue was dissolved in 10 μl ethanol for withdrawing
samples for analysis. The effects of different parameters on the
radiochemical yield of 125I-MNPP were investigated in several
experiments: changing reaction time, temperature, catalysts and different
amounts of each catalyst. 5-125I-MNPP, yield: 80%. t½: 37.50 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no solvent, optimization study, optimized on time,temp., alternative
reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
