$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Labeling of 5-Cl-MNPP with Na125I in organic solvents. All experiments
were carried out in a convenient round bottom flask (5 ml) with two
necks. One of the two necks was fitted with a reflux condenser and the
other one was fitted with rubber stopper for withdrawing samples. The
flask was immersed in an oil bath thermostatically controlled. In this
round bottom flask, 10 μl Na125I (3.7 MBq) was dried by a vacuum line. To
this residue 1 ml of different organic solvents containing 5 mg of
5-Cl-MNPP were added. The reaction mixture was stirred with a magnetic
stirrer and heated to reflux to study the effect of different organic
solvents on the radiochemical yield. 5-125I-MNPP, yield: 80%, solvent:
DMSO. t½: 21.50 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on solvent,time, alternative reaction
conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
