$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Halide Exchange Procedure To a solution of 1.0 g heterocyclic
aryl chloride in 10 mL THF was added 2 mL 4 M HCl in 1,4-dioxane. After 5
min, the solvent was removed and the precipitate dried under reduced
pressure. The hydrochloride salt and 4.0 g NaI previously dried at 120 °C
under vacuum were suspended 30 mL anhyd MeCN and refluxed for 24 h. After
cooling to r.t., an aq solution of 10% K2CO3 and 5% NaHSO3 (10 mL) was
added and the mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic
layers were dried over MgSO4 and the solvents were evaporated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by chromatography on silica
gel using hexanes:EtOAc:Et3N (100:10:1) as the mobile phase if not stated
otherwise. 4-Iodoquinoline (2)13 Chromatography purification of the
residue gave a colorless oil (1.4 g, 91%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Acid-mediated halogen exchange in heterocyclic arenes. A highly effective
iodination method
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wolf, Christian; Tumambac, Gilbert E.; Villalobos, Cristina N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (12), 1801-1804

