$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Copper-Catalyzed Conversion of Aryl Bromides
into Aryl Iodides. In a nitrogen-filled glovebox, CuI (15 mg, 0.079mmol,
5 mol %), NaI (450mg, 3.00mmol), and an aryl bromide (1.5 mmol) were
weighed into an oven-dried microwave tube containing a small stir bar.
Acetonitrile (0.6 mL) was added by syringe. Then
trans-N,N'-dimethylcyclohexane-1,2-diamine (23.7 μL, 0.1 mmol, 10 mol %)
was added by positive displacement pipet, the sample was stirred, and a
septum-lined cap was added. The initial reaction mixture appeared as a
yellow or yellow-green liquid over a white solid. After removing the tube
from the box, the reaction was performed in a CEM Discover microwave
reactor for 30-120 min at 100 °C and 250W (with power adjustments to
maintain temperature), with a 2 min ramp time. After cooling, the
reaction mixture contained a turquoise-blue liquid over a solid. After
cooling, the product mixture was purified by column chromatography on
silica. The yields reported did not take into account the trace amount of
aryl bromide present in the isolated products. 4-Iodotoluene (Table 1,
entry 1). Following the general procedure, 4-bromotoluene (187 μL, 1.5
mmol) was converted to 4-iodotoluene in 60 minutes. The product was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel (10:90 v/v EtOAc :
hexanes). The desired product as a clear liquid that was further purified
by rotary evaporation into white crystals (90% yield, 96% purity). Mp: 34
- 37 °C (lit: 33-35 °C). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.56 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
2H), 6.92 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 2.29 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
137.44, 137.19, 131.18, 90.18, 21.02.1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydrodehalogenation of Aryl Chlorides and Aryl Bromides Using a
Microwave-Assisted, Copper-Catalyzed Concurrent Tandem Catalysis
Methodology
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cannon, Kathleen A.; Geuther, Meagan E.; Kelly, Colin K.; Lin, Shirley;
MacArthur, Amy H. Roy
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2011), 30(15), 4067-4073

