$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Halide Exchange Procedure To a
solution of 1.0 g heterocyclic aryl chloride in 10 mL THF was added 2 mL
4 M HCl in 1,4-dioxane. After 5 min, the solvent was removed and the
precipitate dried under reduced pressure. The hydrochloride salt and 4.0
g NaI previously dried at 120 °C under vacuum were suspended 30 mL anhyd
MeCN and refluxed for 24 h. After cooling to r.t., an aq solution of 10%
K2CO3 and 5% NaHSO3 (10 mL) was added and the mixture was extracted with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and the
solvents were evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified
by chromatography on silica gel using hexanes:EtOAc:Et3N (100:10:1) as
the mobile phase if not stated otherwise. 4-Iodo-2-methylquinoline (6)
Chromatography purification of the residue using hexanes: EtOAc:Et3N
(100:20:1) as the mobile phase gave a white solid (1.2 g, 80%). 1H NMR: δ
= 2.70 (s, 3 H), 7.56 (ddd, J= 1.4 Hz, J= 6.9 Hz, J= 8.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.71
(ddd, J = 1.4 Hz, J= 6.9 Hz, J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.91 (s, 1 H), 7.94 (dd,
J= 1.4 Hz, J= 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.97 (dd, J= 1.4 Hz, J= 8.2 Hz, 1 H). 13C
NMR: δ = 24.6, 112.1, 127.1, 128.4, 129.1, 130.3, 131.32, 133.3, 147.3,
158.6. EI-MS (70 eV): m/z (%) = 269 (100) [M+], 142 (93) [M+ - I], 127
(33) [M+ - I, - Me]. Anal. Calcd for C10H8IN: C, 44.64; H, 3.00; N, 5.21.
Found: C, 44.98; H, 2.78; N, 5.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Acid-mediated halogen exchange in heterocyclic arenes. A highly effective
iodination method
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wolf, Christian; Tumambac, Gilbert E.; Villalobos, Cristina N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (12), 1801-1804

