$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A representative experiment of stoichiometric
C-F bond forming reactions with aryl-CuIII-CuIIIX complexes 1Cl, 1Br and
1I and using several equivalents of AgF is herewith explained. All
reagents used are weighted in vials using a precision balance
(legibility: 0.01 mg) and then entered into an inert-atmosphere glove box
to perform the reaction. Then, 10 mL of CH3CN are added to a vial that
contains 9.5 mg of complex 1Cl (0.025 mmols). The resultant suspension
was transferred to a vial that contains 25.4 mg of AgF (0.2 mmols), which
was vigorously stirred for 8h. Then 50 μL of 1,3,5-trimethoxybenzene 3 mM
were added to the mixture crude. The resultant solution was centrifuged
in order to remove most of solid inorganic salts. Drops of NH4OH were
added to the mixture crude and the solution was dried with MgSO4 and
filtered. The solution was evaporated under vacuum and the solid obtained
was dried under vacuum for several hours. 1H-NMR yield of the C-F
coupling product (L1-F) was obtained in DMSO-d6 and was calculated using
1,3,5-trimethoxybenzene as internal standard. L1-F. Yield 76%; compound
2. Yield 20%. L1-F: 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 400MHz) δ, ppm: 7.08 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
2H, Hb), 6.99 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H, Ha), 3.91 (s, 4H, Hc,Hd), 2.38 (t, J =
6 Hz, 4H, He, Hf), 2.21 (t, J = 6 Hz, 4H, Hi, Hj), 2.10 (s, 2H, Hamines),
1.90 (s, 3H, CH3), 1.56 (quint., J = 6 Hz, 4H, Hg and Hh); 13C-NMR
(CDCl3, 100.6 MHz) δ, ppm: 160.9 (d, JC-F = 244.7 Hz, C1), 130.1 (d, JC-F
= 5.7 Hz, C3), 128.01 (d, JC-F = 14.4 Hz, C2), 123.2 (d, JC-F = 3.9 Hz,
C4), 55.6 (C8), 49.0 (d, JC-F = 2.1 Hz, C5), 43.9 (C6), 40.1 (C9), 26.9
(C7); 19F-NMR (CDCl3, 282.4 MHz) δ, ppm: -124.5 ppm; ESI-MS (CH3CN, m/z):
266.1 (100) [C15H25N3F]+. Anal. Calcd for L1-F·1/5(NH4OH) (%) 66.14 C,
16.46 N, 9.25 H, found: 65.87 C, 16.44 N, 9.15 H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, slow addition of AgF solution, 4% of unidentified product
also obtained, addition of water resulted in reduced yield of the halide
exchange product
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nucleophilic Aryl Fluorination and Aryl Halide Exchange Mediated by a
CuI/CuIII Catalytic Cycle
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
