$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM n-BuLi (2.3 M, 0.139 mL) and n-Bu2Mg (1.0 M, 0.321 mL) were charged into
a nitrogen-filled reaction tube at r.t. A solution of halopyridine (0.8
mmol) in THF (0.76 mL) was added dropwise to the n-Bu3MgLi solution at
-10 °C and the mixture was stirred at -10 °C for 1 h. The resulting
mixture was added to a solution of SO2Cl2 (0.096 mL, 1.2 mmol) in toluene
(0.76 mL) at -10 °C and the mixture was stirred for 10 min. Products:
5a(6-Bromo-2-pyridine-sulfonyl Chloride), Yield: 74 %, and
6(2-bromo-6-chloropyridine).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions shown, alternative Grignard reagents
iPrMgCl or iPrMgCl/LiCl gave lower yield and other product ratio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient and scalable synthesis of pyridine sulfonamides
